import{t as e}from"./utils-COoNfFoj.js";var t={slug:`strategy-breakdowns`,influencerName:`Strategy Breakdowns`,influencerHandle:`@StrategyBreakdowns`,influencerAvatarUrl:`${e}/strategy-breakdowns-avatar.png`,heroDescription:`“Reddit Radar made me realize the bigger opportunity with Perplexity Computer isn’t just automation — it’s orchestration. I wasn’t stitching together APIs, configuring infrastructure, or managing workflows across five different tools. I described the outcome once, and the system handled everything behind the scenes — from content generation to scheduling to syncing and delivery. That’s what an actual operating system for AI work feels like, and why I think this category becomes especially powerful for high-leverage knowledge workers.”`,assetTitle:`Reddit Radar`,screenshotUrl:`${e}/strategy-breakdowns.png`,remixUrl:`https://reddit-radar.pplx.app/#/`,promptTitle:`Try Strategy Breakdown's prompt`,promptText:`Build me a web app that scans these 20 subreddits every morning, pulls the top visual posts from the last 24 hours, and shows them in a feed where I can Save (push to my Notion content ideas DB) or Skip. Use my brand colours [hex codes]. Set up a recurring task to run the scan every morning at 6am London time and email me a summary. Deploy it to a live pplx.app subdomain with no deployment or infrastructure management required on my end. Add an Ideate tab that uses my Anthropic Claude API to generate 5 hook angles per saved post (curiosity, contrarian, data-led, story, listicle) and push them into the Notion page under a ‘Hooks’ heading. Fix the mobile sidebar issue by adding a responsive hamburger menu. Every saved post should arrive in my Notion queue with 5 draft hooks ready so the workflow goes from ‘this image is cool’ to ‘I have a draft’ in under a minute. If connector errors happen because published pplx.app web apps can’t directly access Notion or Gmail APIs from the sandbox, don’t stop at the limitation. Refactor the architecture automatically so save intents queue locally in SQLite and the scheduled 6am recurring task flushes them to Notion and Gmail when connector access is available. Route around platform constraints automatically instead of surfacing them as blockers. Add a Sources tab that lets me toggle subreddits on or off and suggests new relevant subreddits. Make the scan parameters configurable so I can adjust the number of posts pulled and the time window scanned.”`};export{t as default};
